 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hi, how have you been?",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.76,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_05"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Good, good. Thanks.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.73,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_23"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "My coffee from the drip machine always tastes bitter. What am I doing wrong?",
   "est_sec": 4.44,
   "gap_before": 0.3,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "coffee.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "A few things can cause that. Are you using pre-ground coffee, and how long does it sit on the hot plate?",
   "est_sec": 6.61,
   "gap_before": 0.62,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Pre-ground, and it sits there most of the morning.",
   "est_sec": 2.89,
   "gap_before": 0.71,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "coffee.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "That's likely it. The hot plate keeps cooking the coffee, which makes it bitter. Try pouring it into a thermos right after brewing.",
   "est_sec": 7.23,
   "gap_before": 0.41,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Oh, I'd never have guessed that. Anything else?",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 1.01,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "coffee.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Clean the machine with vinegar every month or so. Old oils and scale build up and taste awful.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 1.19,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I don't think I've ever",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.33,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "coffee.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "descaled it, to be honest.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 2.28,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "coffee.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Then you'll probably notice a big difference. Run a couple of rounds of plain water afterwards to rinse it.",
   "est_sec": 5.99,
   "gap_before": 0.96,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg2"
  }
